# Advance Payment Feature

Add an optional **Advance Payment** field that lets customers pay an amount upfront. The advance payment is **deducted from the total**, and the receipt displays the advance paid and the remaining **Balance Due**.

**Current total formula:**
```
total = subtotal - discount + shippingFee + pendingAmount
```

**New total formula (no change to `total`):**
```
total = subtotal - discount + shippingFee + pendingAmount   // stays the same
balanceDue = total - advancePayment                         // NEW derived value
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The `total` field in the database stays unchanged — it represents the invoice total before advance deduction. The **balance due** is calculated at display time as `total - advancePayment`.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Data Layer

#### [MODIFY] [index.ts](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/types/index.ts)

Add `advancePayment` field to the [Invoice](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/types/index.ts#13-26) interface:

```diff
 export interface Invoice {
   ...
   pendingAmount: number;
+  advancePayment: number;
   date: string;
   user_id?: string;
 }
```

---

#### [NEW] Supabase Migration SQL

A new migration to add the `advance_payment` column:

```sql
ALTER TABLE invoices ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS advance_payment decimal(10,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0;
```

> [!NOTE]
> You will need to run this SQL in your Supabase SQL Editor manually, same as the previous migrations.

---

### Storage Layer

#### [MODIFY] [storage.ts](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/utils/storage.ts)

- **[saveInvoice](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/utils/storage.ts#23-53)** — include `advance_payment` in insert payload
- **[updateInvoice](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/utils/storage.ts#125-165)** — include `advance_payment` in update payload
- **[getInvoiceByNumber](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/utils/storage.ts#90-124)** — map `advance_payment` → `advancePayment` in the returned object

---

### UI Components

#### [MODIFY] [SalesReceipt.tsx](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/components/SalesReceipt.tsx)

1. Add new state: `advancePaymentAmount` (same pattern as `discountAmount`)
2. Add input field labeled **"Advance Payment"** in the totals section (after Pending Amount, before the final total box)
3. Update [generateReceipt](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/components/SalesReceipt.tsx#226-303) to include `advancePayment` in the invoice object
4. Display **Balance Due** below the total if an advance payment is entered
5. Reset `advancePaymentAmount` in [handleNewReceipt](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/components/SalesReceipt.tsx#304-318)
6. Populate `advancePaymentAmount` when loading/editing an invoice

---

#### [MODIFY] [ReceiptPreview.tsx](file:///d:/Bill-Kulshan/bill-receipt-generator-main/src/components/ReceiptPreview.tsx)

In the **Totals** section of the receipt, add (after the Total row):

```
Advance Payment:    -LKR X,XXX.XX    (shown in green, only if > 0)
─────────────────────────────────────
Balance Due:         LKR X,XXX.XX    (bold, highlighted)
```

This will appear in the PDF, PNG, and print output automatically since they all render the same `#receipt-content` element.

---

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification

Since there are no automated tests in this project, the changes will be verified manually in the browser:

1. **Run the dev server** → `npm run dev` in the project root
2. **Create an invoice WITHOUT advance payment**:
   - Enter customer name, add items, optionally set discount/courier/pending
   - Generate receipt → confirm the receipt looks the same as before (no advance line shown)
3. **Create an invoice WITH advance payment**:
   - Enter customer name, add items, enter an advance payment amount (e.g., 500)
   - Confirm the total display shows: Total, then Advance Payment subtracted, then Balance Due
   - Generate receipt → confirm the receipt shows "Advance Payment: -LKR 500.00" and "Balance Due: LKR X,XXX.XX"
4. **Export** the receipt as PDF, PNG, and Print — confirm advance payment details are included
5. **Edit an existing invoice** — confirm advance payment loads correctly when searching by invoice number
6. **Run the Supabase migration** — add the `advance_payment` column via SQL Editor
